2a927e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}34 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -29\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536406} {:answer/id #uuid "99ee16dd-f5ce-5d55-9f57-ac836de565b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -27\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536530} {:answer/id #uuid "a35b201c-f9c8-5ef5-99f4-35d4c0535194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}46 & 77 \\\\ 77 & 21\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536547} {:answer/id #uuid "f3949942-a93b-5278-9bdf-682422d7e809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536674} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef71c07-ba83-5d64-938a-f5aa72763b99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536804}] :question/id #uuid "5926666e-0db3-5dee-9762-40fbc13f71e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-138627" :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $B$ in the mean-deviation form above, where the individual observations are given in columns. \nFind the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{4-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 42\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f060f18-5f38-57d0-8035-ee521e1efa10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536447} {:answer/id #uuid "63f36174-881c-57cb-888e-5b635ad28017" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536456} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9c88b3-2c09-54a3-99c5-91c575160cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536463} {:answer/id #uuid "82ed669f-a9bd-5e1c-8760-9d608342f7c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536499} {:answer/id #uuid "e3398816-b77b-5ead-950a-9a70459413a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536447} :answer-field/id #uuid "63610fdd-4a0f-5e58-8e91-40c9b79c1b2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536744}] :question/id #uuid "d39bfe0e-e6e3-509a-9ccb-2651e206d7a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-138639" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample covariance matrix of the data." :question/worked-solution "Recall that  the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC=\\frac{1}{n-1}B{B}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nSo, we first need to compute the mean-deviation form of our observation matrix.\n\nThe sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample covariance matrix is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\frac{1}{3-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 42\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Covariance Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162096 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161909 :question/id #uuid "bdef2fdc-0a38-5bfa-9bc6-7ca50e8c10ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-9835" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d9617e549830347cdd014ce812011ed679a95c576ea2920a93fdc4f09a824b55.svg)\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n![](images/11/11679f410212ead297737ff3a6aaf5a8b2d8daba21abcb1199224857a14d3484.svg)\n\nis given by \n\n![](images/b7/b79eadc9e62263e563c3b385a3fe6dcb3eff75e9667cf9dbb7ccdb47c76ff12d.svg)\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{b}_i = \\mathbf{x}_i - \\mathbf{m}$ for $i = 1,2, \\ldots, n,$ and $\\mathbf{m}$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n![](images/3b/3bdd31917808dd86f0b247fba185f0f8f916412b9e86b1135ceb3a11f2c0ac1a.svg)\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n![](images/a7/a7d9c53005a25972fe250eafc83343434d213cb24ce883c1a6083966bcc39126.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e91708c9-67e2-5228-84fd-1f4ea60064ac" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1992f01f-9787-5991-8f07-c542a44b2013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512157} {:answer/id #uuid "1c6d92ea-4f1e-56e7-878a-54a61789a2b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512160} {:answer/id #uuid "29bb63a6-1e69-50a0-8eec-34dab87c0ea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512194} {:answer/id #uuid "5dc5a73a-1e0e-58fc-855d-8bc21714321a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512319} {:answer/id #uuid "b52309b5-e519-5c28-a0f7-1a897f42f5e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512157} :answer-field/id #uuid "84404952-a965-51e3-9ab4-430762ee3adc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159320}] :question/id #uuid "22493cd3-4d2e-5c66-bb31-313c49c59d2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-137296" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162358 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b23785e-59c3-5c8b-a7cc-6a257ed32da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512200} {:answer/id #uuid "4e971735-2555-5c2e-bdb4-f467bf99cf12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512272} {:answer/id #uuid "631442a5-3529-5b28-b80d-ea82910b12bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512334} {:answer/id #uuid "baee0313-3aa9-58bc-a651-9d7d64343bda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512547} {:answer/id #uuid "e2da0a70-ad5b-56e8-a291-1aa3b5630162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512200} :answer-field/id #uuid "a34b484a-c298-5baa-a88b-4834839a72f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159350}] :question/id #uuid "a6f656ec-c43b-57fd-ba21-5aa8a0f97292" :question/math-academy-id "q-138610" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}21 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d61031c-4423-50f9-9efb-1452f6b1952b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512232} {:answer/id #uuid "81c17eac-92ca-59f1-b6be-d25f5b5973a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512402} {:answer/id #uuid "89d6aeda-7054-5e32-a74a-0e2ca343b3d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512421} {:answer/id #uuid "a389c464-59e1-5313-a31f-2255742146be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512483} {:answer/id #uuid "c48aab5b-9b99-510a-a4db-cb8c07a9b5a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512572} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cd35d7c-3dff-56b6-ae44-55a4d6ea096b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512747}] :question/id #uuid "52c2be5d-881c-537a-9b60-cd461ebff8ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-138609" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}11 & 13 & 15 \\\\ 10 & 7 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}39 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512933 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44e9ff8e-9005-5662-92b6-2423d657e0b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512242} {:answer/id #uuid "4a84cf80-9ac6-550c-9cf0-410296323c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512257} {:answer/id #uuid "748097f9-a18e-56b6-8d3d-fbd3e7580604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512374} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb61e4f-bff1-5ded-88cc-c64443477ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512707} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe7ebd9-1482-50a1-accc-9e0e26fccee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512374} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e40b0a9-1361-5dd4-aab2-b04b18adc043" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512768}] :question/id #uuid "c1c1c9b0-94ce-5a76-9444-4ee707ea7768" :question/math-academy-id "q-138607" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "801331b6-d1a4-5072-8af1-2b93b2ebefc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512401} {:answer/id #uuid "86f71e12-ebbe-5491-b113-0c7da13d21c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512411} {:answer/id #uuid "c81e532d-af9a-57e2-b63d-acd0722b13be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512583} {:answer/id #uuid "ed76a43b-1de2-586d-a13a-82bab00dc68c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512674} {:answer/id #uuid "fc97fbb2-6b7d-542c-ad48-76d5092ef42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512583} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c612bcd-820c-5cdc-80d7-637ac5af81c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512807}] :question/id #uuid "fd960ab2-8677-5176-9a5c-025cfe279786" :question/math-academy-id "q-138613" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 23 & 16 \\\\ 14 & 20 & 20\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ 54\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}23 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57509c8b-6b98-51aa-9762-9963caf04358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536435} {:answer/id #uuid "581f54a2-60c9-5dc5-bb4d-f8f318fe2d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536440} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4429f4-c191-50e8-be52-084fe635f47b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536488} {:answer/id #uuid "bfecac8a-fa87-5d62-a946-7f122c1e66c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536585} {:answer/id #uuid "f1218c8e-974e-52d6-b624-68fd43f78159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536585} :answer-field/id #uuid "b518b34a-8d6e-54eb-93d9-d3cb5a0505b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536774}] :question/id #uuid "6a4bb009-1382-5d80-b122-5cf6749f1552" :question/math-academy-id "q-138615" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536875 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e278261-12a2-522a-865f-2ee4f991690d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536414} {:answer/id #uuid "95c87fe0-b27d-523b-b97f-283a3892f373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536522} {:answer/id #uuid "ad6e45b4-0d19-5a65-9da0-878c4f37d052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536562} {:answer/id #uuid "c24f6fe3-8f3b-5e4f-87ee-cd603ef7bb00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536590} {:answer/id #uuid "c4625cbc-5b19-59bd-9eb5-2085cc809466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536562} :answer-field/id #uuid "9980a067-163c-5305-b9d5-aeb44a51e2ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536761}] :question/id #uuid "b9e3535a-6a10-557b-a90a-dcbee5f059a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-138608" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & ⋯ & {x}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis given by \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}| & | &  & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & ⋯ & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | &  & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${b}_{i}={x}_{i}-m$ for $i=1,2,…,n,$ and $m$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that  \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{1}{3}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-m=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-m=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-m=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean-Deviation Form of an Observation Matrix"}] :topic/math-academy-id 3138 :topic/title "The Sample Covariance Matrix"}]}
